From a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f9012345678 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:15:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] mac80211: add ath11k driver memory reduction and regdomain improvements

Incorporate four key ath11k driver patches from the Jio AX6000 community:
1. 954: Make external IRQ control idempotent to avoid IRQ disable depth masking.
2. 955: Use private page-frag caches for RXDMA rings to eliminate page fragmentation leaks.
3. 959: Present merged FCC regulatory domain with lower 5GHz widened to 160MHz @ 30dBm.
4. 999: Slashes RXDMA buffer ring (4096->2048) and monitor rings (4096->256), reclaiming
   ~35 MB of kernel DMA RAM on 512MB Qualcomm IPQ95xx routers.

Signed-off-by: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Sandeep Sondagar <sandeepsondagar@gmail.com>
